course: dictionary
lesson: 9323
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the dictionary lists them as 1), 2) and 3). To find the right one, read the words around it, as you would with any new word. «It is impossible to flatten the surface of a sphere onto paper without tearing it.» You cannot flatten a ball, so sphere here means a round solid shape.
explain: Sphere can also mean an area of activity, interest or power, as in the sphere of science. Then it is not a shape at all. Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about something round, or about a field of life or knowledge? The clues tell you which.
explain: The third meaning comes from science: a layer around the Earth, as in atmosphere and hemisphere. «A free bubble always becomes a sphere, because it holds the air inside with the smallest surface.» Here the bubble is the clue, because it tells you the shape.
fact: Sphere means a round solid shape like a ball, where every point on the surface is the same distance from the centre.
fact: Sphere can also mean an area of activity, interest or power, such as the sphere of science.
fact: In maths, a sphere is a 3-D shape with one curved face, no edges and no vertices.
fact: Balls, bubbles and planets are nearly spheres.
fact: Hemisphere means half of a sphere, such as half of the Earth.
exercise: «It is impossible to flatten the surface of a sphere onto paper.» What is a sphere here? | A square box | An area of interest, like the sphere of art | *A round solid shape like a ball | A flat piece of paper
exercise: «A free bubble always becomes a sphere.» What shape is a bubble? | A flat circle | A square box | A long tube | *A round ball shape
exercise: Mia says, «The sphere of science is a round shape.» What does sphere mean in this sentence? | A layer of air around a bubble | A round solid shape | Half of a bowl | *An area of activity or interest, like a field of knowledge
test: Which word means half of a sphere, such as half of the Earth? | Spherical | *Hemisphere | Atmosphere | Circle
test: Which shape has one curved face, no edges and no vertices? | A cone | *A sphere | A pyramid | A cube
exam: Sam reads, «The school council has a small sphere of influence.» Which meaning fits best? | A round ball | Half of a bowl | A layer around the Earth | *An area of power or activity
